== Usage ==
This section covers general usage.

=== Loading a Request ===
To load a wiki request into the tool, find the request url or id (either one will work).
Entered the url/id into the box next to the button that says "Populate", then click the button or press Return.

=== Choosing a Template ===
Under the section titled "Template Fields" there is a dropdown labeled "Template", use this dropdown to choose a template.
<br>
See [[#making-a-template|Making a Template]] to find out how to make a template.

== Settings==
Settings for pwr-gen can be found at [[Special:MyPage/pwr/settings.json]].<br>
A settings page with default settings looks like this:
<pre>
{
    "default_template": "default",
    "template_path": "/templates/"
}
</pre>
The <code>default_template</code> specifies the name of the default template.<br>
The <code>template_path</code> specifies the path to your templates.<br>

If no template with the default template name is found, then the global default template is used.
The same occurrs if no settings page is found.

== Templates ==
This section covers making and customizing review templates.

=== Changing the Default ===
The global default template is [[User:Person0192837465/pwr/templates/default]], feel free to shamelessly steal my templates, no attribution necessary.

You can change the default template by editing your [[Special:MyPage/pwr/settings.json|settings page]].

=== Making a Template ===
To make a template, create a subpage of your template path (the default is [[Special:MyPage/pwr/templates/TEMPLATENAME]]).

All pages under your template path will appear in the template dropdown, but subpages of templates will not.

For detailed information about the format of template pages, see https://github.com/tsj845/miraheze-pwr-gen/tree/main/spec/templates.txt.

When writing templates you'll need to keep the following in mind:
* any timestamp or signature must use a canonical parameter to avoid premature substitution.
* any single pair of curly braces that is not a parameter invocation is illegal in the template content.

The template consists of two parts. The first is the template content, which is just wikitext with parameter invocations.
The second is the parameter definitions. These parts are separated by a line containing only <code>{=defs}</code>.

==== Parameters ====
There are two types of parameters, canonical and template-defined. Canonical parameters are always available and always have consistent meanings.

The following is a list of all cononical parameters:
{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Parameter !! Description
|-
| <code>=pageid</code> || a value that can be used as a link target to the wiki request
|-
| <code>=sitename</code> || the requested site name
|-
| <code>=domain</code> || the requested wiki url
|-
| <code>=requester</code> || the username of the account making the request
|-
| <code>=private</code> || "Y" if the request is for a private wiki, "N" otherwise
|-
| <code>=realperson</code> || "Y" if the request is for a wiki covering a real person or group, "N" otherwise
|-
| <code>=nsfw</code> || "Y" if the request is for a wiki that will have NSFW content, "N" otherwise
|-
| <code>=body</code> || the request
|-
| <code>=sig</code> || always has a value of three tildes (this may change to immediately expanding to your signature)
|-
| <code>=sigts</code> || always has a value of four tildes (this may change to immediately expanding to your signature and a timestamp)
|-
| <code>=ts</code> || always has a value of five tildes (this may change to immediately expanding to a timestamp)
|}

Template-defined parameters allow you to add custom fields to the template, making it easy to fill out. Template-defined parameters cannot start with <code>=</code>.

Parameter definitions look like this:
<pre>
define <parameter-type> <parameter-name>
 <property-name> <property-value>
 ...
</pre>

Each parameter type has different allowed properties.

==== Constant Parameters ====
Constant parameters are template-defined parameters with a value defined in the template rather than by user input, their names must begin with <code>:</code>.<br>
{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Property !! Description !! Required
|-
| <code>value</code> || the value of this parameter || Yes
|}
The primary conceived use of constant parameters is as a workaround for single brackets being illegal in template content.

==== Text Parameters ====
Text parameters accept text inputs, and can be single or multiline.
{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Property !! Description !! Required
|-
| <code>default</code> || see the list of standard meanings || No
|-
| <code>display</code> || see the list of standard meanings || No
|-
| <code>essay</code> || default "false", if it is "true" then this parameter accepts multiple lines || No
|-
| <code>ro-if-udf</code> || see the list of stanard meanings || No
|-
| <code>nd-if-udf</code> || see the list of stanard meanings || No
|-
| <code>nd-if-def</code> || see the list of stanard meanings || No
|}

==== Choice Parameters ====
Choice parameters are dropdowns.
{| class="wikitable"
|-
! Property !! Description !! Required
|-
| <code>default</code> || see the list of standard meanings || No
|-
| <code>display</code> || see the list of standard meanings || No
|-
| <code>value</code> || this can appear multiple times, each instance of the property is an option in the dropdown || Yes
|-
| <code>ro-if-udf</code> || see the list of stanard meanings || No
|-
| <code>nd-if-udf</code> || see the list of stanard meanings || No
|-
| <code>nd-if-def</code> || see the list of stanard meanings || No
|}

==== Standard Meanings ====
This is a list of the standard meanings of parameter properties.

; <code>default</code>
: the default value of this parameter
; <code>display</code>
: what this parameter is labelled to the user (defaults to the parameter name)
; <code>ro-if-udf</code>
: this property may appear multiple times, each instance is a parameter name, if all parameters are default this parameter is hidden and forced to be its default value
; <code>nd-if-udf</code>
: this property may appear multiple times, each instance is a parameter name, if any are default this parameter cannot be its default value
; <code>nd-if-def</code>
: this property may appear multiple times, each instance is a parameter name, if any are not default this parameter cannot be its default value

The <code>ro-if-udf</code> parameter takes priority over the <code>nd-if-udf</code> and <code>nd-if-def</code> parameters.

